window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b280-46fe8528daeb252b.json"]={sha256:"46fe8528daeb252bfd446032b102db6007ad19381483ff7aea7f409a722c8f1c",value:{"id":"b280","title":"洪水預報與水庫聯合操作","titleEn":"Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"將預報誤差、河道傳播時間、庫容與下游通洪能力放在同一個運算框架，練習集合機率、校準、預洩與衝突限制辨識。教材以兩座假想水庫展示聯合操作所需的狀態和責任邊界，計算結果只作方法教學，實際操作仍需正式規程與有權機關決策。","summaryEn":"Place forecast uncertainty, routing time, storage and downstream capacity in one calculation framework. Exercises cover ensemble probabilities, calibration, prerelease and conflicting constraints. Two hypothetical reservoirs illustrate the states and responsibilities required for coordinated operation. Results teach methods rather than authorize releases; real decisions require approved operating rules, current observations and the responsible institutions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["集合超越機率","Ensemble exceedance probability"],["機率預報的布里爾分數","Brier score for probability forecasts"],["匯流點的同步疊加","Aligned flows at a junction"],["預洩所需時間窗","Time window for prerelease"],["預報改善與獨立驗證","Forecast improvement and independent validation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["集合超越機率","機率預報的布里爾分數","匯流點的同步疊加","預洩所需時間窗","預報改善與獨立驗證"],"labelsEn":["Ensemble exceedance probability","Brier score for probability forecasts","Aligned flows at a junction","Time window for prerelease","Forecast improvement and independent validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「集合超越機率」建立原創假想基準，再以「分位數與有限成員」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless；第二組為 ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：保持 N=20 個等權成員及同一流量門檻，把超越成員 Ne 從 8 增至 10，經驗比例由 0.4 增至 0.5，也就是增加十個百分點。這不是證明真實風險上升同樣幅度，仍須用獨立事件檢驗機率校準。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Ensemble exceedance probability and examine another controlling mechanism through Quantiles with finite ensembles. The first inputs and result are Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless; the second are ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep N=20 equally weighted members and the same flow threshold, increasing exceedances Ne from 8 to 10. The empirical fraction rises from 0.4 to 0.5, an increase of ten percentage points. This does not prove an equal change in true risk; probability calibration still requires independent events.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b280-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「集合超越機率」與「分位數與有限成員」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" and \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-01","title":"集合超越機率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集合超越機率」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ensemble exceedance probability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。這些成員不一定相互獨立，也可能共享降雨偏差，因此比例不是自然界真實機率的保證。門檻必須對應同一地點、時段與流量定義，瞬時峰值不能與日平均混用。操作比較應同時看後果與機率，並透過過往未參與校準的事件檢查可靠度，而不是只選最樂觀的成員作決策依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集合超越機率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. Members may be dependent or share rainfall bias, so the fraction is not a guarantee of nature's true probability. Match location, lead period and discharge definition; instantaneous peaks differ from daily means. Compare consequences as well as probabilities, and evaluate reliability on events excluded from calibration instead of basing decisions on the most optimistic member. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ensemble exceedance probability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集合超越機率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ensemble exceedance probability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-01-k1","title":"集合超越機率","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability","text":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。這些成員不一定相互獨立，也可能共享降雨偏差，因此比例不是自然界真實機率的保證。","textEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. Members may be dependent or share rainfall bias, so the fraction is not a guarantee of nature's true probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集合超越機率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" is correct?","options":["集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成","集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent","An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b280-v15-02","title":"集合超越機率：定量估算","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集合超越機率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ensemble exceedance probability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境的經驗比例，非已驗證校準之真實洪水機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Empirical fraction of equally weighted scenarios, not a demonstrated calibrated probability of flooding. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境的經驗比例，非已驗證校準之真實洪水機率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Empirical fraction of equally weighted scenarios, not a demonstrated calibrated probability of flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集合超越機率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ensemble exceedance probability\", which statement holds?","options":["水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b280-v15-03","title":"集合超越機率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集合超越機率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ensemble exceedance probability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。用獨立歷史預報回放分組比較預報機率和實際發生頻率，保留漏報與誤報紀錄，並確認沒有事後雨量被偷偷加入當時預報。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Use independent forecast replays to compare probability groups with observed frequencies, retaining misses and false alarms and ensuring later rainfall observations were not inserted into earlier forecasts. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持二十個等權成員，將超越數增加到十個重算比例。說明需要哪些歷史樣本才能檢查這個機率是否可靠，並列出成員相關可能造成的限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep twenty equally weighted members and increase exceedances to ten. Recalculate the fraction, identify historical samples needed to test reliability, and describe limitations caused by dependence between ensemble members across the forecast set.","failure":"注意干擾：集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。用獨立歷史預報回放分組比較預報機率和實際發生頻率，保留漏報與誤報紀錄，並確認沒有事後雨量被偷偷加入當時預報。","textEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Use independent forecast replays to compare probability groups with observed frequencies, retaining misses and false alarms and ensuring later rainfall observations were not inserted into earlier forecasts.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持二十個等權成員，將超越數增加到十個重算比例。說明需要哪些歷史樣本才能檢查這個機率是否可靠，並列出成員相關可能造成的限制。","textEn":"Keep twenty equally weighted members and increase exceedances to ten. Recalculate the fraction, identify historical samples needed to test reliability, and describe limitations caused by dependence between ensemble members across the forecast set.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集合超越機率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ensemble exceedance probability\"?","options":["固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":0,"explanation":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b280-v15-04","title":"集合超越機率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集合超越機率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ensemble exceedance probability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。若只用集合範圍當絕對上下界，會掩蓋共同模式誤差，需以獨立事件檢查可靠度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Treating its range as an absolute physical bound conceals shared model error, requiring reliability checks against independent observed events. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作比較應同時看後果與機率，並透過過往未參與校準的事件檢查可靠度，而不是只選最樂觀的成員作決策依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare consequences as well as probabilities, and evaluate reliability on events excluded from calibration instead of basing decisions on the most optimistic member.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。若只用集合範圍當絕對上下界，會掩蓋共同模式誤差，需以獨立事件檢查可靠度。","textEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Treating its range as an absolute physical bound conceals shared model error, requiring reliability checks against independent observed events.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集合超越機率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b280-v15-05","title":"分位數與有限成員：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「分位數與有限成員」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Quantiles with finite ensembles” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。分位數描述預報分布的位置，不是平均值的信賴區間，也不是所有可能洪水的上限。比較不同系統時應保留相同分位數定義、權重與有效時段，並報告成員數。操作評估還需檢視完整歷線，因為單一峰值分位數可能無法代表水量和峰值到達時間之間的關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分位數與有限成員」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. A quantile locates a forecast distribution; it is neither a confidence interval for the mean nor a bound on every possible flood. Preserve definitions, weights and valid periods when comparing systems, and report member count. Examine complete hydrographs because a peak quantile alone may miss relationships between flood volume and arrival time that matter for storage decisions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Quantiles with finite ensembles” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分位數與有限成員」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Quantiles with finite ensembles”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-05-k1","title":"分位數與有限成員","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles","text":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。分位數描述預報分布的位置，不是平均值的信賴區間，也不是所有可能洪水的上限。","textEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. A quantile locates a forecast distribution; it is neither a confidence interval for the mean nor a bound on every possible flood.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分位數與有限成員」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\" is correct?","options":["九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。"],"optionsEn":["The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b280-v15-06","title":"分位數與有限成員：定量估算","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分位數與有限成員」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Quantiles with finite ensembles” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。適用邊界：指定線性插值經驗分位數，五個成員不能證明尾部分布校準。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Specified linearly interpolated empirical quantile; five members do not establish tail calibration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。適用邊界：指定線性插值經驗分位數，五個成員不能證明尾部分布校準。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Specified linearly interpolated empirical quantile; five members do not establish tail calibration.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分位數與有限成員」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b280-v15-07","title":"分位數與有限成員：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分位數與有限成員」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Quantiles with finite ensembles” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。用另一種常見分位數定義做差異檢查，若高分位變動大，應報成員有限造成的不穩定，而不是隱藏選法。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Compare an alternative quantile convention. Large high-quantile differences should be reported as finite-ensemble instability rather than concealed by an undocumented choice of method. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把最高成員改成每秒二百立方公尺重算同一分位數，其他值與定義不變。說明單一成員敏感度如何影響解讀，並保留原始情境供水量分析。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only the largest member to two hundred cubic metres per second and recompute the same quantile. Explain sensitivity to one member and retain complete scenarios for subsequent flood-volume analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。用另一種常見分位數定義做差異檢查，若高分位變動大，應報成員有限造成的不穩定，而不是隱藏選法。","textEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Compare an alternative quantile convention. Large high-quantile differences should be reported as finite-ensemble instability rather than concealed by an undocumented choice of method.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把最高成員改成每秒二百立方公尺重算同一分位數，其他值與定義不變。說明單一成員敏感度如何影響解讀，並保留原始情境供水量分析。","textEn":"Change only the largest member to two hundred cubic metres per second and recompute the same quantile. Explain sensitivity to one member and retain complete scenarios for subsequent flood-volume analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分位數與有限成員」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b280-v15-08","title":"分位數與有限成員：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分位數與有限成員」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Quantiles with finite ensembles” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。應標示此為摘要包絡，不能當成一個一致情境。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Label such a curve as a summary envelope rather than treating it as one dynamically consistent forecast scenario. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作評估還需檢視完整歷線，因為單一峰值分位數可能無法代表水量和峰值到達時間之間的關係。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine complete hydrographs because a peak quantile alone may miss relationships between flood volume and arrival time that matter for storage decisions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。應標示此為摘要包絡，不能當成一個一致情境。","textEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Label such a curve as a summary envelope rather than treating it as one dynamically consistent forecast scenario.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分位數與有限成員」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b280-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「機率預報的布里爾分數」與「水庫時段水量守恆」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" and \"Reservoir interval water balance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-09","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「機率預報的布里爾分數」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brier score for probability forecasts” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。評估事件必須使用相同門檻與預報提前時間，並包含未發生洪水的情況，否則會扭曲分數。不同地區的基準發生率會影響比較，因此還需與適當參考預報對照。可靠度、辨識度及資料不足的問題應分開診斷，避免把一個平均分數當作完整風險認證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機率預報的布里爾分數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. Lower values generally indicate better matching but do not directly measure the loss from each decision. Use consistent thresholds and lead times and include non-events; selecting only floods distorts the score. Different base rates also affect comparisons, requiring an appropriate reference forecast. Diagnose reliability, discrimination and sample limitations separately rather than treating one average score as complete certification of operational risk or forecast quality. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brier score for probability forecasts” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「機率預報的布里爾分數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brier score for probability forecasts”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-09-k1","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts","text":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。評估事件必須使用相同門檻與預報提前時間，並包含未發生洪水的情況，否則會扭曲分數。","textEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. Lower values generally indicate better matching but do not directly measure the loss from each decision.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「機率預報的布里爾分數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" is correct?","options":["布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b280-v15-10","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：定量估算","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機率預報的布里爾分數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brier score for probability forecasts” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。適用邊界：四筆獨立保留樣本的示範平均，不代表已完成長期服務驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Illustrative average for four held-out cases, not validation of a long-term forecasting service. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。適用邊界：四筆獨立保留樣本的示範平均，不代表已完成長期服務驗證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Illustrative average for four held-out cases, not validation of a long-term forecasting service.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「機率預報的布里爾分數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brier score for probability forecasts\", which statement holds?","options":["下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b280-v15-11","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機率預報的布里爾分數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brier score for probability forecasts” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。另報事件數、非事件數及基準分數，分提前時間比較，避免把較容易的短期預報混入後宣稱長期能力改善。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Report event and non-event counts with reference scores, separating lead times so easier short-range cases do not create a misleading claim of long-range improvement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把第三筆機率從零點六改成零點八，其餘不變重算分數。說明這次改善為何不能保證所有未來事件都較好，並提出需增加的樣本分層方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the third probability from zero point six to zero point eight and recalculate. Explain why improvement on this case does not guarantee future performance, then propose additional strata for evaluating a larger sample.","failure":"注意干擾：只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。另報事件數、非事件數及基準分數，分提前時間比較，避免把較容易的短期預報混入後宣稱長期能力改善。","textEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Report event and non-event counts with reference scores, separating lead times so easier short-range cases do not create a misleading claim of long-range improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把第三筆機率從零點六改成零點八，其餘不變重算分數。說明這次改善為何不能保證所有未來事件都較好，並提出需增加的樣本分層方式。","textEn":"Change the third probability from zero point six to zero point eight and recalculate. Explain why improvement on this case does not guarantee future performance, then propose additional strata for evaluating a larger sample.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「機率預報的布里爾分數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brier score for probability forecasts\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b280-v15-12","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機率預報的布里爾分數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brier score for probability forecasts” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。若評估資料由結果篩選，應重新建立完整發布紀錄。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. An outcome-selected evaluation needs rebuilding from the complete issue archive, including dates on which the event did not occur. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：可靠度、辨識度及資料不足的問題應分開診斷，避免把一個平均分數當作完整風險認證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Diagnose reliability, discrimination and sample limitations separately rather than treating one average score as complete certification of operational risk or forecast quality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。若評估資料由結果篩選，應重新建立完整發布紀錄。","textEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. An outcome-selected evaluation needs rebuilding from the complete issue archive, including dates on which the event did not occur.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「機率預報的布里爾分數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b280-v15-13","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「水庫時段水量守恆」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reservoir interval water balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。時段兩端流量線性變化時可用梯形積分，若洪峰在中間突起，端點平均便可能漏算重要水量。蒸發、取水與溢流應依時間尺度決定是否列入，省略時需明示。庫容還必須透過現行水位容量曲線與觀測對照，不能把高程差直接當成體積差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水庫時段水量守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. Trapezoidal integration is appropriate for linearly changing endpoint flows, but can miss an interior peak. Include or explicitly neglect evaporation, withdrawals and spill according to the time scale. Compare storage with observations through a current stage-storage relation, because elevation change is not itself a volume change and sediment accumulation can alter that relation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reservoir interval water balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水庫時段水量守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reservoir interval water balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-13-k1","title":"水庫時段水量守恆","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance","text":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。時段兩端流量線性變化時可用梯形積分，若洪峰在中間突起，端點平均便可能漏算重要水量。","textEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. Trapezoidal integration is appropriate for linearly changing endpoint flows, but can miss an interior peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水庫時段水量守恆」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reservoir interval water balance\" is correct?","options":["水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加","聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase","Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b280-v15-14","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：定量估算","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水庫時段水量守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reservoir interval water balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。適用邊界：時段流量線性變化且無其他水量項，僅求庫容增量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Applicable boundary: Linearly changing flows without other water terms; calculates storage increment only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。適用邊界：時段流量線性變化且無其他水量項，僅求庫容增量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Applicable boundary: Linearly changing flows without other water terms; calculates storage increment only.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水庫時段水量守恆」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reservoir interval water balance\", which statement holds?","options":["目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b280-v15-15","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水庫時段水量守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reservoir interval water balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。分列取水、洩漏及溢流，若殘差集中在洪峰時，應查取樣頻率與測站延遲，不先任意修改入流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. List withdrawals, leakage and spill. Peak-centred residuals require checking sampling and station delays before arbitrarily adjusting inflow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將時段縮短一半而保留相同端點流量假設，重算庫容增量並說明線性假設改變了什麼。再加入一個時段中間峰值，提出更適合的積分方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve the interval while retaining the endpoint-flow assumptions and recompute storage change, explaining the altered linear trajectory. Add an interior peak and propose an integration approach that can capture its volume.","failure":"注意干擾：流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。分列取水、洩漏及溢流，若殘差集中在洪峰時，應查取樣頻率與測站延遲，不先任意修改入流。","textEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. List withdrawals, leakage and spill. Peak-centred residuals require checking sampling and station delays before arbitrarily adjusting inflow.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將時段縮短一半而保留相同端點流量假設，重算庫容增量並說明線性假設改變了什麼。再加入一個時段中間峰值，提出更適合的積分方式。","textEn":"Halve the interval while retaining the endpoint-flow assumptions and recompute storage change, explaining the altered linear trajectory. Add an interior peak and propose an integration approach that can capture its volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水庫時段水量守恆」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reservoir interval water balance\"?","options":["先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b280-v15-16","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水庫時段水量守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reservoir interval water balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。應先做量綱與時間同步檢查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Check dimensions and synchronized timing before interpreting apparent storage residuals as physical leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：庫容還必須透過現行水位容量曲線與觀測對照，不能把高程差直接當成體積差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare storage with observations through a current stage-storage relation, because elevation change is not itself a volume change and sediment accumulation can alter that relation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。應先做量綱與時間同步檢查。","textEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Check dimensions and synchronized timing before interpreting apparent storage residuals as physical leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水庫時段水量守恆」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reservoir interval water balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b280-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「匯流點的同步疊加」與「下游剩餘通洪額度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Aligned flows at a junction\" and \"Residual downstream flow allowance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-17","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「匯流點的同步疊加」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aligned flows at a junction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。支流洪峰可能與水庫洩流錯峰或疊峰，傳播過程也有蓄水與波形變化。本單元只在已演算到同一斷面同一時刻的流量上做守恆相加，明確把路由工作放在前置條件。操作比較應保存每股貢獻歷線，才能追溯下游超限來自哪個時段和來源。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「匯流點的同步疊加」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. Tributary peaks can coincide or separate, while channel storage changes timing and shape. This unit adds contributions already routed to one section and instant, explicitly treating routing as a prerequisite. Preserve each contribution hydrograph so a downstream exceedance can be traced to its source and release period rather than to a misleading simultaneous upstream sum. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aligned flows at a junction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「匯流點的同步疊加」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aligned flows at a junction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-17-k1","title":"匯流點的同步疊加","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction","text":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。支流洪峰可能與水庫洩流錯峰或疊峰，傳播過程也有蓄水與波形變化。","textEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. Tributary peaks can coincide or separate, while channel storage changes timing and shape.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「匯流點的同步疊加」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Aligned flows at a junction\" is correct?","options":["同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b280-v15-18","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：定量估算","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「匯流點的同步疊加」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aligned flows at a junction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。適用邊界：三股流量已演算至同一匯流斷面同一時刻，未在此假設原始洩流同步。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Applicable boundary: All contributions are routed to the same junction and instant; upstream releases are not assumed simultaneous here. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。適用邊界：三股流量已演算至同一匯流斷面同一時刻，未在此假設原始洩流同步。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Applicable boundary: All contributions are routed to the same junction and instant; upstream releases are not assumed simultaneous here.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「匯流點的同步疊加」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Aligned flows at a junction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b280-v15-19","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「匯流點的同步疊加」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aligned flows at a junction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。用匯流點實測流量核對合計，並保留河段儲水及側向流入項，避免把差額全歸成某座水庫計量誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Compare their sum with junction observations, retaining reach storage and lateral inputs instead of assigning every residual to one reservoir's meter error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將支流到達流量增加二十立方公尺每秒重算合計，再把其峰值提前一小時畫出歷線。說明沒有河道路由資料時，哪些聯合操作結論仍無法成立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase arriving tributary flow by twenty cubic metres per second and recalculate the sum, then shift its peak one hour earlier on a hydrograph. Identify coordination conclusions that remain unsupported without routing information.","failure":"注意干擾：若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。用匯流點實測流量核對合計，並保留河段儲水及側向流入項，避免把差額全歸成某座水庫計量誤差。","textEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Compare their sum with junction observations, retaining reach storage and lateral inputs instead of assigning every residual to one reservoir's meter error.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將支流到達流量增加二十立方公尺每秒重算合計，再把其峰值提前一小時畫出歷線。說明沒有河道路由資料時，哪些聯合操作結論仍無法成立。","textEn":"Increase arriving tributary flow by twenty cubic metres per second and recalculate the sum, then shift its peak one hour earlier on a hydrograph. Identify coordination conclusions that remain unsupported without routing information.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「匯流點的同步疊加」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Aligned flows at a junction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b280-v15-20","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：失效診斷","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「匯流點的同步疊加」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aligned flows at a junction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。需查到達時間分布與預報誤差，而非只比較各水庫的最大出流值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Examine arrival-time uncertainty rather than comparing only the maximum outflow from each reservoir separately. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作比較應保存每股貢獻歷線，才能追溯下游超限來自哪個時段和來源。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preserve each contribution hydrograph so a downstream exceedance can be traced to its source and release period rather than to a misleading simultaneous upstream sum.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。需查到達時間分布與預報誤差，而非只比較各水庫的最大出流值。","textEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Examine arrival-time uncertainty rather than comparing only the maximum outflow from each reservoir separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「匯流點的同步疊加」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Aligned flows at a junction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b280-v15-21","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「下游剩餘通洪額度」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual downstream flow allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。把它轉成水庫出流需要路由、設備能力與爬升限制，也要面對預報誤差。若其他來源已超過限制，負餘額代表該假設組合無法靠非負洩流解決，不能隨意截成零後宣稱安全。規則來源與權責必須清楚，教材僅比較假想限制的數學含義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游剩餘通洪額度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. Routing, outlet capacity, ramp limits and forecast uncertainty intervene before converting it to release. If other sources already exceed the limit, a negative allowance signals infeasibility under the assumptions; clipping it to zero does not restore safety. Identify rule authority and provenance while treating the numerical limit here only as a hypothetical teaching condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual downstream flow allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游剩餘通洪額度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual downstream flow allowance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-21-k1","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance","text":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。把它轉成水庫出流需要路由、設備能力與爬升限制，也要面對預報誤差。","textEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. Routing, outlet capacity, ramp limits and forecast uncertainty intervene before converting it to release.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游剩餘通洪額度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Residual downstream flow allowance\" is correct?","options":["下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b280-v15-22","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：定量估算","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游剩餘通洪額度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual downstream flow allowance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。適用邊界：給定假想斷面限制與同步到達流量，不是實際核准洩流量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Hypothetical section limit with aligned arriving flows, not an authorized reservoir release. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。適用邊界：給定假想斷面限制與同步到達流量，不是實際核准洩流量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Hypothetical section limit with aligned arriving flows, not an authorized reservoir release.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游剩餘通洪額度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Residual downstream flow allowance\", which statement holds?","options":["情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b280-v15-23","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游剩餘通洪額度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual downstream flow allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。對預報支流做敏感度範圍，使用路由模型檢查水庫能否形成目標到達流量，並確認設備及正式操作規程是否允許。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Use routing to examine whether a reservoir can produce the target arriving flow, then check equipment constraints and formally approved operating rules. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將支流到達流量提高到每秒二百五十立方公尺，重算餘額並說明負值意義。列出應回報的限制衝突，而不是自行創造一個看似可行的非負數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise tributary arrival to two hundred fifty cubic metres per second and recompute the allowance. Explain a negative result and list the conflicting conditions to report rather than inventing an apparently feasible nonnegative value.","failure":"注意干擾：若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。對預報支流做敏感度範圍，使用路由模型檢查水庫能否形成目標到達流量，並確認設備及正式操作規程是否允許。","textEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Use routing to examine whether a reservoir can produce the target arriving flow, then check equipment constraints and formally approved operating rules.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將支流到達流量提高到每秒二百五十立方公尺，重算餘額並說明負值意義。列出應回報的限制衝突，而不是自行創造一個看似可行的非負數字。","textEn":"Raise tributary arrival to two hundred fifty cubic metres per second and recompute the allowance. Explain a negative result and list the conflicting conditions to report rather than inventing an apparently feasible nonnegative value.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游剩餘通洪額度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Residual downstream flow allowance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b280-v15-24","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游剩餘通洪額度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual downstream flow allowance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。限制也可能隨堤防或下游施工改變，必須確認版本與有效範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Limits may also depend on current downstream conditions, requiring version and validity checks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：規則來源與權責必須清楚，教材僅比較假想限制的數學含義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify rule authority and provenance while treating the numerical limit here only as a hypothetical teaching condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。限制也可能隨堤防或下游施工改變，必須確認版本與有效範圍。","textEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Limits may also depend on current downstream conditions, requiring version and validity checks.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游剩餘通洪額度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Residual downstream flow allowance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b280-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「預洩所需時間窗」與「不相容操作限制」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Time window for prerelease\" and \"Incompatible operating constraints\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-25","title":"預洩所需時間窗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「預洩所需時間窗」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time window for prerelease” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。可用時間窗還受下游容量、設備爬升、環境要求與預報可靠度影響，不能只用目標體積除最大閘流量。若入流在窗口內增加，淨庫容形成速度會降低；若將來降雨落空，保留供水也有代價。教材以固定額外淨釋放量建立時間尺度，實際方案必須透過完整情境與授權規則比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預洩所需時間窗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The available window depends on downstream capacity, ramping, environmental requirements and forecast reliability, not just maximum gate flow. Increasing inflow reduces net storage creation, while a missed storm creates water-supply tradeoffs. This example uses a fixed additional net release to establish a time scale; real alternatives require full scenarios and authorized rules, not direct execution of the arithmetic. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Time window for prerelease” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預洩所需時間窗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Time window for prerelease”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-25-k1","title":"預洩所需時間窗","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease","text":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。可用時間窗還受下游容量、設備爬升、環境要求與預報可靠度影響，不能只用目標體積除最大閘流量。","textEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The available window depends on downstream capacity, ramping, environmental requirements and forecast reliability, not just maximum gate flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預洩所需時間窗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Time window for prerelease\" is correct?","options":["目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行","預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan","Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b280-v15-26","title":"預洩所需時間窗：定量估算","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預洩所需時間窗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time window for prerelease” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。適用邊界：額外淨釋放已扣相對基準入流變化，假設可持續且無爬升時間。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Applicable boundary: Additional net release already accounts for inflow change relative to baseline, assuming sustained feasibility and no ramp time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。適用邊界：額外淨釋放已扣相對基準入流變化，假設可持續且無爬升時間。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Applicable boundary: Additional net release already accounts for inflow change relative to baseline, assuming sustained feasibility and no ramp time.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預洩所需時間窗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Time window for prerelease\", which statement holds?","options":["預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。"],"optionsEn":["The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b280-v15-27","title":"預洩所需時間窗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預洩所需時間窗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time window for prerelease” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。核對窗口內下游條件與爬升限制，對降雨提前、延後或未發生情境分別演算，並保存決策使用的預報版本。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Check downstream conditions and ramps, replay early, late and absent rainfall scenarios, and preserve the forecast version used for comparison. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將額外淨釋放降到每秒四十立方公尺重算時間，再加入兩小時逐步爬升。說明為何須積分實際增量歷線，並列出方案比較需要的正式限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce additional net release to forty cubic metres per second and recalculate time, then introduce a two-hour ramp. Explain why the actual incremental hydrograph needs integration and list formal constraints required for comparing alternatives.","failure":"注意干擾：如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。核對窗口內下游條件與爬升限制，對降雨提前、延後或未發生情境分別演算，並保存決策使用的預報版本。","textEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Check downstream conditions and ramps, replay early, late and absent rainfall scenarios, and preserve the forecast version used for comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將額外淨釋放降到每秒四十立方公尺重算時間，再加入兩小時逐步爬升。說明為何須積分實際增量歷線，並列出方案比較需要的正式限制。","textEn":"Reduce additional net release to forty cubic metres per second and recalculate time, then introduce a two-hour ramp. Explain why the actual incremental hydrograph needs integration and list formal constraints required for comparing alternatives.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預洩所需時間窗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Time window for prerelease\"?","options":["建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b280-v15-28","title":"預洩所需時間窗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預洩所需時間窗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time window for prerelease” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。預報延後發布時，原先看似足夠的窗口也可能消失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A later forecast issue can also remove a previously available window, invalidating the earlier feasibility calculation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教材以固定額外淨釋放量建立時間尺度，實際方案必須透過完整情境與授權規則比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This example uses a fixed additional net release to establish a time scale; real alternatives require full scenarios and authorized rules, not direct execution of the arithmetic.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。預報延後發布時，原先看似足夠的窗口也可能消失。","textEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A later forecast issue can also remove a previously available window, invalidating the earlier feasibility calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預洩所需時間窗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Time window for prerelease\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b280-v15-29","title":"不相容操作限制：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「不相容操作限制」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Incompatible operating constraints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。這個結果應揭露限制衝突，不能由程式默默刪除較難滿足的條件。某些規則可能有正式優先序或應變程序，但作者不能自行發明權限。模型需保留各限制的來源、有效時間與物理意義，分辨設備能力不足、下游容量衝突及資料錯誤，讓有權人員能檢查並作成可追溯決策。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「不相容操作限制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. If the largest lower bound exceeds the smallest upper bound, no common feasible value exists. Report that conflict rather than silently discarding a difficult condition. Formal priorities or emergency procedures may apply, but a model author cannot invent authority. Retain each bound's source, valid period and physical meaning to distinguish equipment limits, downstream conflicts and data errors, enabling responsible personnel to make a traceable decision. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Incompatible operating constraints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「不相容操作限制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Incompatible operating constraints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-29-k1","title":"不相容操作限制","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints","text":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。這個結果應揭露限制衝突，不能由程式默默刪除較難滿足的條件。","textEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. If the largest lower bound exceeds the smallest upper bound, no common feasible value exists.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不相容操作限制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Incompatible operating constraints\" is correct?","options":["求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。"],"optionsEn":["Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Several rules can become release bounds for one interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b280-v15-30","title":"不相容操作限制：定量估算","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「不相容操作限制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Incompatible operating constraints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。適用邊界：正缺口表示所給同時限制無交集，未自動放寬任何規則。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A positive gap means the simultaneous stated bounds have no intersection; no rule is automatically relaxed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。適用邊界：正缺口表示所給同時限制無交集，未自動放寬任何規則。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A positive gap means the simultaneous stated bounds have no intersection; no rule is automatically relaxed.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不相容操作限制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Incompatible operating constraints\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b280-v15-31","title":"不相容操作限制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「不相容操作限制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Incompatible operating constraints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。若無解，檢查是否誤把不同時段或不同斷面限制混合，確認後輸出衝突清單及責任窗口，不以數值平滑掩蓋問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. For infeasibility, check mixed periods or sections before producing a conflict list and responsible review route rather than smoothing the numbers to hide it. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把第二下界改成每秒九十五立方公尺，重新求交集並說明可行範圍。再列一個資料時段不一致造成假衝突的例子，設計能攔下它的前置檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the second lower bound to ninety five cubic metres per second and find the feasible interval. Construct a false conflict caused by mismatched time periods and design a preprocessing check that would catch it.","failure":"注意干擾：優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。若無解，檢查是否誤把不同時段或不同斷面限制混合，確認後輸出衝突清單及責任窗口，不以數值平滑掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. For infeasibility, check mixed periods or sections before producing a conflict list and responsible review route rather than smoothing the numbers to hide it.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把第二下界改成每秒九十五立方公尺，重新求交集並說明可行範圍。再列一個資料時段不一致造成假衝突的例子，設計能攔下它的前置檢查。","textEn":"Change the second lower bound to ninety five cubic metres per second and find the feasible interval. Construct a false conflict caused by mismatched time periods and design a preprocessing check that would catch it.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不相容操作限制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Incompatible operating constraints\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b280-v15-32","title":"不相容操作限制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「不相容操作限制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Incompatible operating constraints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。必須檢查求解狀態及每條限制殘差，不能只看目標函數有改善。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Inspect solver status and every constraint residual rather than judging success solely by an improved objective value. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模型需保留各限制的來源、有效時間與物理意義，分辨設備能力不足、下游容量衝突及資料錯誤，讓有權人員能檢查並作成可追溯決策。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retain each bound's source, valid period and physical meaning to distinguish equipment limits, downstream conflicts and data errors, enabling responsible personnel to make a traceable decision.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。必須檢查求解狀態及每條限制殘差，不能只看目標函數有改善。","textEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Inspect solver status and every constraint residual rather than judging success solely by an improved objective value.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不相容操作限制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Incompatible operating constraints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem."],"answer":2,"explanation":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b280-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「情境違反率與風險」與「預報改善與獨立驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" and \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-33","title":"情境違反率與風險：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「情境違反率與風險」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scenario violation rate and risk” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。此比例取決於情境權重、代表性與相關性，不等於已知真實風險，也未描述超限幅度。少數很嚴重的失敗可能比多次輕微超限更重要，因此應同時報告頻率、最大值、持續時間及涉及對象。增加集合成員只改善抽樣解析度的一部分，若共同模型偏差未修正，風險估計仍會系統性失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「情境違反率與風險」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The fraction depends on weights, representativeness and dependence; it is not a known true risk and says nothing about severity. A few severe failures may matter more than many slight exceedances, so report frequency, magnitude, duration and affected receptors together. More members refine only part of sampling resolution and cannot by themselves remove shared model bias or an omitted failure mechanism. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scenario violation rate and risk” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「情境違反率與風險」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scenario violation rate and risk”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-33-k1","title":"情境違反率與風險","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk","text":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。此比例取決於情境權重、代表性與相關性，不等於已知真實風險，也未描述超限幅度。","textEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The fraction depends on weights, representativeness and dependence; it is not a known true risk and says nothing about severity.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「情境違反率與風險」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" is correct?","options":["聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b280-v15-34","title":"情境違反率與風險：定量估算","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「情境違反率與風險」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scenario violation rate and risk” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境違反比例，沒有將百分之六宣稱成核准風險或真實機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Equally weighted scenario violation fraction, not an approved risk level or established true probability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境違反比例，沒有將百分之六宣稱成核准風險或真實機率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Equally weighted scenario violation fraction, not an approved risk level or established true probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「情境違反率與風險」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scenario violation rate and risk\", which statement holds?","options":["九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b280-v15-35","title":"情境違反率與風險：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「情境違反率與風險」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scenario violation rate and risk” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。另檢查高後果但低頻情境是否被抽樣遺漏，以保留事件回放測試共同偏差，並明示若成員有權重時應改用加權比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Examine omitted rare but consequential cases and replay held-out events for common bias. If members carry weights, explicitly replace the simple count with weighted probability. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持三個違反情境但將集合增加到六十個重算比例，說明為何不能據此自動宣稱更安全。為三個情境補上不同超限幅度和時間，提出更完整比較表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep three violating scenarios but enlarge the ensemble to sixty and recalculate the fraction without automatically claiming greater safety. Assign different magnitudes and durations to the three cases and construct a more informative comparison table.","failure":"注意干擾：把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。另檢查高後果但低頻情境是否被抽樣遺漏，以保留事件回放測試共同偏差，並明示若成員有權重時應改用加權比例。","textEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Examine omitted rare but consequential cases and replay held-out events for common bias. If members carry weights, explicitly replace the simple count with weighted probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持三個違反情境但將集合增加到六十個重算比例，說明為何不能據此自動宣稱更安全。為三個情境補上不同超限幅度和時間，提出更完整比較表。","textEn":"Keep three violating scenarios but enlarge the ensemble to sixty and recalculate the fraction without automatically claiming greater safety. Assign different magnitudes and durations to the three cases and construct a more informative comparison table.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「情境違反率與風險」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scenario violation rate and risk\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b280-v15-36","title":"情境違反率與風險：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「情境違反率與風險」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scenario violation rate and risk” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。若只報比例而刪除歷線，決策者便無法辨認真正需要應變的後果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Reporting only the fraction while discarding hydrographs prevents reviewers from identifying consequences that require a distinct response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：增加集合成員只改善抽樣解析度的一部分，若共同模型偏差未修正，風險估計仍會系統性失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: More members refine only part of sampling resolution and cannot by themselves remove shared model bias or an omitted failure mechanism.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。若只報比例而刪除歷線，決策者便無法辨認真正需要應變的後果。","textEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Reporting only the fraction while discarding hydrographs prevents reviewers from identifying consequences that require a distinct response.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「情境違反率與風險」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b280-v15-37","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「預報改善與獨立驗證」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Forecast improvement and independent validation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。不同事件、提前時間及流量大小必須公平配對，否則看似改善可能只是測試樣本更容易。校準與驗證要按時間或事件分開，避免同一場洪水的相鄰資料同時進入訓練與測試。平均指標還可能掩蓋洪峰時間或極端事件表現，因此應搭配事件分層與操作後果回放，才能判斷改善是否對聯合調度有用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預報改善與獨立驗證」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. Match events, lead times and flow regimes fairly; an easier test sample can mimic improvement. Separate calibration and validation by time or event so neighbouring records from one flood do not leak across sets. Average scores may hide peak-timing or extreme-event errors, requiring stratified evaluation and operational replays before claiming that better forecasting improves coordinated reservoir decisions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Forecast improvement and independent validation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預報改善與獨立驗證」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Forecast improvement and independent validation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-37-k1","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation","text":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。不同事件、提前時間及流量大小必須公平配對，否則看似改善可能只是測試樣本更容易。","textEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. Match events, lead times and flow regimes fairly; an easier test sample can mimic improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預報改善與獨立驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\" is correct?","options":["預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b280-v15-38","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預報改善與獨立驗證」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Forecast improvement and independent validation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。適用邊界：同四筆保留樣本與正參考誤差，改善尺度不等於風險降低百分比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Same four held-out cases with positive reference error; skill is not a percentage reduction in operational risk. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。適用邊界：同四筆保留樣本與正參考誤差，改善尺度不等於風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Same four held-out cases with positive reference error; skill is not a percentage reduction in operational risk.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預報改善與獨立驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\", which statement holds?","options":["只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b280-v15-39","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預報改善與獨立驗證」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Forecast improvement and independent validation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。逐筆列絕對誤差，再按洪峰、低流與提前時間分層；最後用相同規則回放操作，檢查誤差改善是否真正改變庫容或下游結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. List absolute errors and stratify by peaks, low flows and lead time. Replay identical operating rules to test whether better scores actually change storage or downstream outcomes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將模型第三筆誤差降到十二立方公尺每秒重算改善尺度，其他資料不變。說明仍需哪些峰值時序及操作回放結果，才能判定對防洪決策有實際幫助。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce the third model error to twelve cubic metres per second and recompute skill with other values fixed. Identify peak-timing and operating-replay evidence still needed before judging whether the improvement benefits flood decisions.","failure":"注意干擾：用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。逐筆列絕對誤差，再按洪峰、低流與提前時間分層；最後用相同規則回放操作，檢查誤差改善是否真正改變庫容或下游結果。","textEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. List absolute errors and stratify by peaks, low flows and lead time. Replay identical operating rules to test whether better scores actually change storage or downstream outcomes.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將模型第三筆誤差降到十二立方公尺每秒重算改善尺度，其他資料不變。說明仍需哪些峰值時序及操作回放結果，才能判定對防洪決策有實際幫助。","textEn":"Reduce the third model error to twelve cubic metres per second and recompute skill with other values fixed. Identify peak-timing and operating-replay evidence still needed before judging whether the improvement benefits flood decisions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預報改善與獨立驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\"?","options":["保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b280-v15-40","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預報改善與獨立驗證」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Forecast improvement and independent validation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。若模型只改善低流量，也可能未改善最關鍵洪峰操作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Improvements concentrated in low flow may also leave the most consequential flood-peak decisions unchanged. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均指標還可能掩蓋洪峰時間或極端事件表現，因此應搭配事件分層與操作後果回放，才能判斷改善是否對聯合調度有用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average scores may hide peak-timing or extreme-event errors, requiring stratified evaluation and operational replays before claiming that better forecasting improves coordinated reservoir decisions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。若模型只改善低流量，也可能未改善最關鍵洪峰操作。","textEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Improvements concentrated in low flow may also leave the most consequential flood-peak decisions unchanged.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預報改善與獨立驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
